-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in McKean County came in under 90% of normal in July to August for 32 of 75 years since 1951, and September to October matched it at 32. In 2025 that middle ran 47% of normal in July to August and 49% in August to September. Grid 26005 had its driest year in 1963 at 73% of normal. For grid 26306 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 reads 109.9, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
